1.2.0: the juice package - superjuice motion front-end

One engine, two front-ends. superjuice reads YUV4MPEG2 on stdin,
renders every frame through libpolajuice with the new temporal axis,
and writes y4m on stdout; FFmpeg pipes handle codecs and audio, so the
engine stays dependency-free (a y4m parser and BT.601 conversion are
the only additions, C420/C444 in, C444 out).

Temporal axis in the core, per-frame and deterministic: gate weave
(subpixel drift in the transport gate, smooth-noise driven), exposure
flicker, and frame-decorrelated boiling grain (seed xor frame). Weave
and flicker are per-camera character - super8 heaviest, autochrome
hand-cranked, technicolor-3strip machine-steady - and only run in
movie mode: stills rendering is bit-identical to 1.1.0, tested. The
frame field also lets the stills CLI render "frame N of a reel".

Front-end shares the film library, compatibility rules, develop and
age with polajuice (resolver extracted to src/cli/filmlib.c); instant
cameras are refused as still-print formats. make builds both binaries;
make check gains an ffmpeg-piped movie test (output gate geometry,
frame count via ffprobe, determinism, seed sensitivity, instant
refusal) that skips cleanly without ffmpeg.
